==Trivia==
*Design-wise, Wild Doge is a [[Doge]] mixed with a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Canyne|Canyne/Palamute]] from the ''Monster Hunter'' series - the tip-off is the white "X" on his forehead.
*Wild Doge's description references the Jack London novel ''[[wikipedia:The Call of the Wild|The Call of the Wild]]'', which details its canine protagonist's transformation during his exposure in nature, ending with him embracing his new life as a feral beast with Canadian wolves.
*The "tropics" where Wild Doge became a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] are implied to be [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]], a sparsely-populated subtropical island that appears as [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|stage 48]] in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]] of [[Empire of Cats]], replaced by the Moon in other versions of the game.
**The term "underlying power of the wild" (野生の底力) in Wild Doge's Japanese description also appears on the [[Media:Ec047 ja.png|tree]] that serves as Iriomote Island's base.
**''[[wikipedia:Awamori|Awamori]]'', the drink mentioned in Wild Doge's Japanese description, is a signature product of [[wikipedia:Okinawa Prefecture|Okinawa]], the Japanese prefecture where Iriomote Island is located.
**Wild Doge appears in [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] and [[Birth of True Man]], which have a [[Media:Rc164.png|similar enemy base]] to Iriomote Island. This is further supported by how [[Humanity Catified]] is the 48th sub-chapter of [[Uncanny Legends]].
***Another Behemoth with a potential connection to this island is [[Crustaceous Scissorex]], whose shell is the skull of a [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]] - an enemy introduced in Chapter 3 Iriomote Island.
*The phrase "a life spent in pursuit of the ultimate wave" in Wild Doge's description may be a reference to [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], implying a connection between the two.
*Along with [[Ragin' Gory]] and [[Ultima Beast Naala]], Wild Doge was one of the three enemies that were updated to have the Behemoth type in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]].
*Wild Doge and Ragin' Gory are the only Behemoths whose Japanese names do not include a title with the format "Super X Beast" (超X獣 ''Chō Xjū''), where X is a prefix related to the enemy in question.
**They are also the only Behemoths to have any hiragana in their Japanese names.

